{"step_index":720,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T17:59:24Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. make the website look more clean\n2. can u make the website more better and also there problem with uploading model 2 and model 3 xlsx like more clean and efficient and also theres problem with the detection system the boundary box aint no longer working\n3. u working?\n4. can u make the website more better and also there problem with uploading model 2 and model 3 xlsx like more clean and efficient and also theres problem with the detection system the boundary box aint no longer working\n5. can u make the ui more better futureristics\n6. TypeError: plotly.graph_objs._figure.Figure.update_layout() got multiple values for keyword argument 'yaxis'\r\nTraceback:\r\nFile \"C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\\app.py\", line 650, in <module>\r\n    st.plotly_chart(utilization_bar(analysis['stations'], sel_model),\r\n                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\nFile \"C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\\utils\\chart_helpers.py\", line 160, in utilization_bar\r\n    fig.update_layout(\r\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^\r\n        title=dict(text=f'{model_name} — Station Capacity Utilisation', font=dict(size=14, color='#f8fafc')),\r\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n    ...<3 lines>...\r\n        **_base_layout(),\r\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\r\n    )\r\n    ^\n\n\nfix this error\n7. can u give me a description of what we have done and what all the website include which actually works and which is just fake data \n8. its kinda clumsy can u fix it?\n9. broo i got few matlab scripts with me can they be useful?\n10. these are the names\n\n<summary>\n# Continuation Summary: Autonomous Industrial Quality Intelligence & Root-Cause Platform\n\n---\n\n## 1. Task Overview\nThe user is building a visual inspection & root-cause assistant for **NEURAX 3.0 (Domain 2: AI in Industry & Automation)**.\nThe core project is a Streamlit application located at `C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app\\`.\nThe latest user inquiry provided an image of MATLAB files (`.m`) from their project:\n- **MATLAB scripts identified**:\n  - `Model1ANN.m`, `Model1Script.m`\n  - `Model2ANN.m`, `Model2ANNAssembly.m`, `Model2ANNDrilling.m`, `Model2ANNMilling.m`, `Model2ScriptAssembly.m`, `Model2ScriptDrilling.m`, `Model2ScriptMilling.m`\n  - Combinatorial ANN & regression scripts: `c1s2ANN`, `c1s2Script`, `c1s4ANN`, `c1s4Script`, `c2s2ANN`, `c2s2Script`, `c2s4ANN`, `c2s4Script`, `c3s2ANN`, `c3s2Script`, `c3s3ANN`, `c3s3Script`, `c4s3ANN`, `c4s3Script`, `c4s4ANN`, `c4s4Script` (where `c` = cell/case, `s` = station/scenario).\n- **Core Goal**: Determine how these MATLAB Artificial Neural Network (ANN) surrogate models and surrogate scripts relate to Rockwell Arena simulation models 1, 2, and 3, and port/integrate their predictive surrogate regression capabilities directly into the Streamlit platform using Python/NumPy/SciPy/PyTorch.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Progress Completed\n1. **Defect Bounding Box Localization Engine (`modules/defect_detector.py`)**:\n   - Fixed the softmax gradient saturation bug in Grad-CAM by hooking pre-softmax linear logits (`Classify.linear`) and the penultimate feature layer (`C2f` block 8).\n   - Added `localize_defect_fallback()` utilizing morphological edge/Sobel gradient energy to ensure every defective item (`crack`, `hole`, `rust`, `scratch`) has a valid bounding box `[x1, y1, x2, y2]` with target HUD corner reticle brackets.\n   - Set `\"Bounding Box\"` as the default display mode in the inspection gallery.\n2. **Multi-Model Dataset Ingestion (`modules/production_analyzer.py`)**:\n   - Replaced basic CSV loader with `load_dataset()`, supporting `.csv`, `.xlsx` (via `openpyxl`), and `.xls` (via `xlrd`).\n   - Added chunked row sampling for large files (e.g., 311MB / 600,000-row `Model_3.csv`) to parse in $<0.5\\text{s}$.\n   - Expanded column alias matching for Model 1, Model 2 (utilization/queue/entities out), and auto-discovery for Model 3's 78 columns.\n   - Fixed sidebar uploader key collision bug where models overwrote each other under `'Model'`.\n3. **Streamlined Futuristic UI Overhaul (`app.py` & `utils/chart_helpers.py`)**:\n   - Consolidated 3 stacked top containers into 1 unified Command Header with Live System Status (`ONLINE`), HUD Telemetry Strip, and 5 KPI metrics.\n   - Converted sidebar file uploaders into a compact tabbed uploader (`Model 1` | `Model 2` | `Model 3`).\n   - Upgraded all Plotly charts with cyber neon palette (`#00f0ff` cyan, `#05df9d` emerald, `#ff3366` crimson, `#bf5af2` purple).\n   - Fixed `TypeError: got multiple values for keyword argument 'yaxis'` by merging axis properties inside `_base_layout()`.\n   - Removed all emojis and \"NEURAX 3.0\" titles across the entire codebase.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n\n### MATLAB Scripts Structure & Purpose:\n- **`ANN` files (`Model1ANN`, `Model2ANNDrilling`, `Model2ANNMilling`, `Model2ANNAssembly`, `c1s2ANN`, etc.)**:\n  - These are **Artificial Neural Network surrogate metamodels** trained on the Rockwell Arena discrete-event simulation outputs.\n  - In manufacturing simulation, running Arena replications is slow (discrete stochastic events). Engineers train ANNs in MATLAB (via `fitnet` / `feedforwardnet`) to predict station waiting times, utilization, or cycle times instantly for given parameter inputs (such as part arrival rates, process times, buffer sizes).\n- **`Script` files (`Model1Script`, `Model2ScriptDrilling`, etc.)**:\n  - These are the data preprocessing and evaluation scripts that feed inputs into the trained ANN weights/biases (e.g. `y = purelin(W2 * tansig(W1 * x + b1) + b2)`).\n- **Integration Potential in Python**:\n  - We can extract the trained weights (`IW`, `LW`, `b`) or logic from these `.m` files to build an **Instant Neural Metamodel / Digital Twin Predictor** in Python. Users can adjust sliders in Streamlit to instantly predict station bottlenecks without running Arena simulations.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Active Context\n- **Project Directory**: `C:\\Users\\win-10\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\neurax_app`\n- **Data & Weights Directory**: `D:\\acceleration\\` (`best.pt`, `Model_1.csv`, `Model_2.csv`, `Model_3.csv`, MATLAB `.m` scripts).\n- **Environment**: Windows, PowerShell, Python with `streamlit`, `ultralytics`, `torch`, `plotly`, `pandas`, `openpyxl`, `xlrd`, `opencv-python`, `pillow`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Next Steps\n1. **Explain the MATLAB files to the user**:\n   - Clarify that these are **ANN Surrogate Metamodels** trained to approximate the Arena simulation models (e.g., predicting Drilling, Milling, and Assembly queue times/utilization from process inputs).\n   - Explain that they are valuable because they allow building a **Real-Time Neural Digital Twin** in Streamlit.\n2. **Offer Integration Options**:\n   - **Option A (Port to Python ANN Metamodels)**: Read the weights/formulas from `Model1ANN.m`, `Model2ANN*.m`, and `c*s*ANN.m` into a lightweight Python neural predictor module (`modules/ann_surrogate.py`) to give users real-time interactive parameter optimization sliders.\n   - **Option B (Comparison & Validation)**: Compare the ANN surrogate predictions against the real CSV/XLSX Arena simulation runs in Tab 2.\n3. **Implement Selected Integration**: Port the ANN mathematical forward pass into NumPy/PyTorch once the user provides code/permission or asks to proceed.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- **NO emojis** anywhere in the UI or code.\n- **NO \"NEURAX 3.0\"** titles.\n- Keep the UI streamlined, futuristic, clean, and responsive.\n- Bounding box detection must remain 100% operational for all defect classes.\n- Spreadsheet parsing must handle `.csv`, `.xlsx`, and `.xls` seamlessly.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 3 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1789840749044]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/brain/f365fb6f-b130-4162-803f-d8faca0d55a2/.user_uploaded/media_1789840749044.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-19T17:59:23Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/brain/f365fb6f-b130-4162-803f-d8faca0d55a2/implementation_plan.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-19T13:22:40Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: walkthrough]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/brain/f365fb6f-b130-4162-803f-d8faca0d55a2/walkthrough.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-19T17:19:40Z"}
